{"changes":["(New) Import a playlist from a USB device into your Collection, with choices to copy missing tracks, import only matching tracks, or cancel the import.","(New) Choose how folder drops handle an existing playlist or folder with the same name: create a copy, replace it, keep it, or ask each time.","(New) Import and export star-rating changes from USB devices.","(New) Add a File Created column to the browser and sort tracks by their file creation date.","(New) Choose the BPM range used for analysis, including automatic analysis during import.","(New) Optionally write analysed or edited track keys to supported audio-file tags.","(New) Create Intelligent Playlists from the playlist tree, and select or clear all playlists at once in Sync Manager.","(New) Clear a hot cue directly from its pad, change its colour from the pad, and continue to the next track automatically in supported one-player layouts.","(Fixed) USB exports and syncs preserve separate device playlists with matching names, handle playlist changes between the device’s two libraries, and work reliably with larger playlists and older players.","(Fixed) USB sync now works on macOS exFAT drives when full filesystem flushing is unavailable, including converted tracks.","(Fixed) Importing or opening USB tracks works more reliably on Linux when filename capitalization differs, and Windows can import MP3s dropped from Explorer onto a playlist.","(Fixed) Auto Relocate can find files moved elsewhere on the same drive and searches folders more like rekordbox.","(Fixed) Linked players can load tracks stored in symlinked library folders, while only the intended library files are exposed.","(Fixed) Hot-cue loops now launch as loops and display their loop ranges; Active Loops appear correctly in the MEMORY list and waveforms.","(Fixed) Tracks stored through rekordbox Cloud Library Sync can play from their Dropbox copy when the original local file is gone.","(Fixed) Analysis keeps precise measured tempos and gives Normal analysis a single constant tempo grid.","(Fixed) XDJ-RX3 Link Export now auto-connects correctly, including rear-USB use on Linux, and linked players receive each hot cue’s own colour.","(Fixed) A deck’s previous and next controls now move through its source list, and Command+Q works correctly on AZERTY keyboards.","(Fixed) Track-list reordering remains reliable while scrolling, including duplicate playlist entries.","(Fixed) rbxport shows its window if the interface fails to finish loading, and the About item works on Linux and Windows.","(Improved) Sync Manager opens with connected devices’ playlist trees visible and restores the prior selection for the first previously synced device.","(Improved) Lists remember their scroll position, and Locate Track Loaded on Deck finds the loaded track more predictably.","(Improved) Analysis failures in the status bar identify the affected tracks and their reasons."]}
